name 'building-data-driven-systems-preassessment-q11_2025'

question 'Which of the following is a primary goal of "Accessibility" in data-driven systems?'

wrong 'Ensuring the website loads in under one second on all devices.'
wrong 'Making sure the data is encrypted so that only the developer can see it.'
right 'Ensuring that users with screen readers can understand the data through proper labels and alt text.'
wrong 'Using the most advanced AI models to generate the user interface automatically.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 7

Accessibility is about removing barriers. In data systems, this means using clear labels, high contrast, and semantic HTML so that assistive technology can interpret the data.
MARKDOWN
